These tests are based on those in tb_preprocessor, but now the preprocessor is embedded between two FIFO buffers.
We are thus also testing synchronization and throttling.

Every test requires observed scenario counts before success. Tests 1-4 require
accepted pass/discard/store commands, finite replay output, and both ordering and
timing check completion. Timing is measured from the first read request; a fatal
watchdog prevents a missing checker from silently hanging or passing early.
Tests 3-4 additionally require a length-one replay. Test 5 requires blocked writes,
replay stalls, checked delivery, and completion of the randomized phase. Test 6
requires all expected replay words to be checked while exercising replay
backpressure. The observer samples the embedded preprocessor's accepted commands
and outputs, rather than counting words merely offered to the ingress FIFO.
